diff --git a/dev_docs/PROGRESS.md b/dev_docs/PROGRESS.md
index 3b15ee8..708056b 100644
--- a/dev_docs/PROGRESS.md
+++ b/dev_docs/PROGRESS.md
@@ -218,6 +218,7 @@ Legend: `[x]` done in code · `[~]` partly done / needs your device to confirm 
 | 0256 | 2026-11-18 | Alloys phase P5b: **Customers** moves onto the router. The Customers screen (search, create, edit) and the customer sheet in the cart (remote search, create) no longer import the Shopify customer file; they ask for the function through `needFeature('customers', ...)` (new `src/alloyhost/need.ts`). With the legacy default that reaches the same Shopify calls with the same inputs, and the screens show the same words when Shopify is not there: the old "Shopify is not set up - open More ▸ Settings ▸ Shopify." without a login, and the old practice-mode message in practice. Once a person has chosen their own setup, the message names the Element instead, and an Alloy that lacks a function (say, no "edit customer") gives a plain "cannot do that" error. One contract change: the customer input carries first and last name separately, as the till asks for them, rather than one name that the Alloy would have to split. The practice-mode branches in the screens are untouched. 5 new tests in `tests/alloyp5customers.test.ts`; full suite 2134 passing. |
 | 0257 | 2026-11-18 | Alloys phase P5c: **Catalogue** moves onto the router. The full import and the half-hourly refresh in `sync.ts` read items, collections and the customer list through `listAllItems`, `listAllCollections` and `listAllCustomers` (new `src/alloyhost/catalogue.ts`), and the Items screen creates and edits items through `needFeature('catalogue', 'createItem' / 'updateItem')`. Against Shopify these make the same calls with the same inputs in the same order (tests compare each against calling Shopify directly, including the stock-count and collection steps of creating an item), and the screens show the same words when Shopify is missing or in practice mode. An Alloy may return a long list in pages: `readAllPages` reads every page and stops with an error if a cursor repeats, so a faulty Alloy cannot loop; Shopify returns each list as one page. The local customer list is optional: with Customers off, or an Alloy that cannot list them all (new optional `listAll`), the till just stores none. The contract gained `onProgress` on a page request (the import's progress line) and `listAll` on Customers. `fetchShop` in Settings is left alone: it is the connection step, which the setup picker (P6) takes over through the Alloy's `connect`. 6 new tests in `tests/alloyp5catalogue.test.ts`; full suite 2140 passing. |
 | 0258 | 2026-11-19 | Alloys phase P5d: **Stock** moves onto the router, **and a gap from 0255 and 0257 is fixed**. Stock: the half-hourly poll asks what changed through `stockChanges` (new `src/alloyhost/stock.ts`, same query, same guards, the cursor now comes back from the Alloy), and Receive, Adjust and Count in Inventory and the Scan stock panel go through `needFeature('stock', 'adjust' / 'set')`, keeping the panel's retry key (Inventory makes a fresh key per tap, as before). On the legacy selection a missing login fails with the old words; with Stock switched off on a chosen setup the poll just skips the step. **The gap:** Shopify network errors are translated to `AlloyNetworkError` at the Alloy boundary, but the app's `isNetworkError` only recognised the Shopify class, so a dropped connection on a routed call (discounts, catalogue) would have set the poll to "error" instead of "offline", and the stock screens' "No connection" branch would have been missed. `isNetworkError` now recognises both, which also covers every later Element. The Shopify-specific `instanceof ShopifyUserError` in the order outbox (`sync.ts`) is not affected yet and is on the list for the Orders step. `AdjustReason` now comes from `alloykit/types` (the old export stays). 7 new tests in `tests/alloyp5stock.test.ts` (including one that a dropped connection reads as a network error through discounts and stock), and the practice-mode pin in `traininginventory.test.ts` follows the new call text. Full suite 2147 passing. |
+| 0259 | 2026-11-19 | Alloys phase P5e: **Gift cards** move onto the router. Every place that touched a gift card in Shopify now asks for it through `needFeature('giftCards', ...)`: Pay (charge and cancel-credit), the cart scan box, the Gift cards screen (balance and history), the new-card sheet, Reports (outstanding liability), the refund flow (original-card credits, which read the whole history first, and refunds to a new card) and the order outbox (cards bought in a sale). Against Shopify the calls and their inputs are identical (tests compare each against calling Shopify directly), including the once-only debit and credit that skip what is already on the card and refuse a different amount, and the recipient on a new card. With no login the screens say the same "not set up" words, and in practice mode the same practice words. **Outbox:** a Shopify refusal now arrives as an Alloy user error, so the check that marks a queued sale "needs attention" (rather than retrying forever) now accepts both kinds. Contract: two optional functions added (`allHistory`, `outstanding`), `verified` and the transaction `id` are required, and the router counts the once-only debit and credit as writes in practice mode. `newGiftCode` (a plain 16-character code maker) moved to `src/lib/giftCode.ts`, with the old export kept; the card type and transaction type now come from `alloykit/types`. The `debitNote` helper in the Shopify folder is still imported by Pay and is on the P9 list with the other plain helpers. 7 new tests in `tests/alloyp5giftcards.test.ts`; two source pins (`giftcardonce`, `trainingrefund`) follow the new call text. Full suite 2154 passing. |
 | 0241 | 2026-11-14 | **B7e, Help pictures for three more pages (your request).** The picture engine (`src/lib/helpFigures.ts`) already drew 12 pages; this adds seven figures drawn from the real screens' labels: Cloud sync (set up, invite link, join, Back up everything and Export all events, which the page did not describe at all), Offline and sync errors (the Support & diagnostics Sync rows, with the new **Last full sync** line explained) and Split and part payments (the Split amount sheet and the Payment screen after a split). 15 of 68 pages now have a figure. No code; `help.json` rebuilt, the 63 help tests pass. Not looked at on a device: the pictures follow the screens' labels but I cannot see the iPad. The other 53 pages are not drawn; the Daily float report is the hardest (it draws notes and coins) and was left. | B7e |
 | 0240 | 2026-11-14 | **B8, review of the gift-card calls before the live test (your request).** Read `giftcards.ts` against Shopify's `giftCardCredit` and `giftCardDebit` pages: the mutations, fields and the `write_gift_card_transactions` scope are as documented. Shopify gives neither call an idempotency key, and the cancel side already looked in the card's history before crediting again, but the **charge did not**: if Shopify took the charge and the reply was lost, the app said "could not be charged", the cashier tapped again and the card was charged twice. New `debitGiftCardOnce` and `src/lib/shopify/giftCardOnce.ts`: the Nth payment of a sale has the same note on every retry (`POS sale <8 chars> tender N`), the card's history is read for it first, and a debit already there is not sent again (Shopify returns a debit as a negative amount, so amounts are compared by size). The credit side now uses the same helper. Pay.tsx charges through it. `tests/giftcardonce.test.ts` (6 tests) pass. DEVICE_TESTS T10 gains the Wi-Fi-off charge test and a check of the notes. **The live run is still yours:** it spends real gift-card value on your store. | B8 |
 | 0239 | 2026-11-11 | **iCloud was slow, and polls could pile up.** Found by reading the code, not measured on a device: the 25 second tick called `pollShared()` straight away with no check for one already running, and the change pushes and the Sync now button call it too. One poll is about twenty iCloud round trips in a row, so on a slow connection it takes longer than 25 seconds and every tick started another, all competing for iCloud and rewriting the same local state; a cash drawer closed on one iPad then took minutes to show on the other. `pollShared` is now single-flight (`src/lib/singleFlight.ts`): a call made while a poll runs joins it. Diagnostics ▸ Sync gains a **Last full sync** line with the total time and the slowest parts (`src/lib/pollTiming.ts`), so the next step is based on real numbers. Not changed, and likely still slow: the poll's steps run one after another, Back up everything and the events export read 100 records per round trip, and the iCloud tab asks iCloud four things in a row to connect. Parallelising the steps is the next lever but needs a look at what each writes first. Not run on a device. `tests/companionjobs`, `logosync` and `noticesync` cannot run in the sandbox (missing modules) and fail the same without this change; their source checks were run by hand and hold. | Sync |
